Topic: PIQ Form (Personal Information Questionnaire) 📄🔥

👉 This is the MOST IMPORTANT document in SSB
👉 It decides ~70% of your interview questions

1️⃣ What is PIQ Form?

👉 A form you fill before interview containing:

Personal details
Education
Family background
Hobbies
Achievements
Responsibilities

👉 Interviewer uses this to analyze your life

2️⃣ Why PIQ is VERY IMPORTANT

👉 Every answer you give in interview comes from PIQ

💥 If you write something → you MUST justify it

3️⃣ Sections of PIQ
🔹 1. Personal Details
Name
Age
Address

👉 Simple, no tricks

🔹 2. Educational Details
Marks (10th, 12th, degree)
Subjects
Performance

👉 Be ready:

Why marks low/high?
Favorite subject?
🔹 3. Family Background
Parents’ occupation
Siblings

👉 They check:

Responsibility
Family influence
🔹 4. Hobbies / Interests (VERY IMPORTANT)

👉 Don’t write fake hobbies ❌

Example:

If you write “Reading”
👉 Be ready:

Which books?
Favorite author?
Last book read?
🔹 5. Achievements

👉 Sports, NCC, competitions

💥 (Your hockey background is BIG advantage 💪)

🔹 6. Responsibilities

👉 Example:

House responsibilities
Team captain
College roles

👉 Shows leadership

4️⃣ How to Fill PIQ (CORRECT WAY)

✅ Be honest
✅ Be clear
✅ Be specific

❌ Wrong

“Hobby: Music”

✅ Correct

“Hobby: Listening to motivational and patriotic songs”

5️⃣ Common Mistakes

❌ Writing fake hobbies
❌ Copying others
❌ Hiding weaknesses
❌ Giving vague answers

6️⃣ PRO STRATEGY (SELECTION SECRET)

👉 Everything in PIQ should show:

Responsibility
Consistency
Growth

💥 PIQ + SDT must match

7️⃣ Expected Interview Questions from PIQ

👉 Examples:

Why low marks in 12th?
Tell me about your hobby
What is your daily routine?
Your role in family?
8️⃣ Practice Task (VERY IMPORTANT)

Prepare answers for:

1️⃣ Your hobby
2️⃣ Your strength
3️⃣ Your weakness
4️⃣ Your daily routine
5️⃣ Why do you want to join defence?

🧠 SECRET TIP

👉 Interviewer is not checking perfection

👉 He checks:

Honesty
Awareness
Confidence

💥 Be REAL = You win

📊 Quick Summary
Section	Focus
Education	Consistency
Family	Responsibility
Hobbies	Genuine interest
Achievements	Performance
Goal	Self-awareness
